<title>BELGIUM: Belgium mulls leaded car fuel ban from 2000.</title>
<headline>Belgium mulls leaded car fuel ban from 2000.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian State Secretary for the Environment Jan Peeters said on Monday he supported a proposed European Commission directive to ban the use of leaded petrol in cars from January 1, 2000.</p>
<p>He made the comment in an answer to a written question from a member of parliament.</p>
<p>The market share of leaded car fuel in Belgium was 31 percent in 1995, down from 92 percent in 1988.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
